<title>USA: Woodhead president concluding treatments.</title>
<headline>Woodhead president concluding treatments.</headline>
<dateline>BUFFALO GROVE, Ill. 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Woodhead Industries Inc said its president and chief executive officer, C. Mark DeWinter, next week will conclude chemotherapy for Hodgkin's disease, a form of lymphatic cancer.</p>
<p>The company disclosed in July that DeWinter was undergoing chemotherapy.</p>
<p>&quot;My cancer is in remission and my doctors have told me I can expect a full and complete recovery,&quot; DeWinter said in a statement. &quot;I feel great, and I look forward to leading our fine Woodhead team in the years to come.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
